We formatted the PSM level quantification tables so that columns match
with those of the annotation and peptide/protein level data. Each PSM level
data turned into \link[SingleCellExperiment:SingleCellExperiment]{SingleCellExperiment} objects including row data
information. All the PSM level assays used to generate \link[QFeatures:QFeatures]{QFeatures} object.

The peptide and protein assays were formatted as \link[SingleCellExperiment:SingleCellExperiment]{SingleCellExperiment}
objects and the sample metadata were matched to the column names. The
objects are then added to the \link[QFeatures:QFeatures]{QFeatures} object and the rows of the PSM
data are linked to the rows of the corresponding peptide data based on the
sequence information through an \code{AssayLink} object. Peptide assays and
protein assays linked in the same way through Gene Symbols as provided by
the authors.
}

